'' A DYNAMIC ARRAY IN COMMON, declared in two modules, is one array. Its descriptor went out
'' with the element size, rank and flags as an initial value, which made it a definition in
'' each module:
''
''     lld-link: error: duplicate symbol: GINTS$
''
'' fbc writes it with no initializer, so before the first redim every field reads 0: the
'' first printed line, 'ubound( a, 0 )' included. Output compared with fbc-modern.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/common-array-main.tiko tests/codegen/src/common-array-other.tiko -o tests/codegen/commonarray.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: duplicate symbol
'' RUN: tests/codegen/commonarray.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  0-1 0-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  4 11 2str 3 2.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  5 6
